// EU07 / 303E main traction circuit, for Knsgf's electric_sim circuit compiler
// (Derail_Valley_electric_concept, CC0 / MIT).
//
// GENERATED by build_circuit.py - change the wiring there, not here.
//
// WIRING: real. Read off sheet 4 of the 303E schemat ideowy (zm. 37) and tested against
// the contactor programme on sheet 3: with every resistor counted as one ohm the
// resistance in circuit falls at every controller step, 30 to 1 over positions 1-27,
// 0 at 28, 7.0 to 0.5 over 29-42, 0 at 43.
//
//   LINE - SL1 - R25 - R5 - [motors 1,2] - M1 - R3 R7 R9 ... R29 - X
//   X - IR2 - earth (parallel)            X - IS - R1 - R2 - N4 (series)
//   LINE - SL3 - IR1 - N4 (parallel)      N4 - R4 R6 ... R26 - Z - [motors 3,4] - M2 - R28 - R30 - earth
//   M1 - IM - Z (the bridge, position 28)
//
// Each SRn bridges its own Rn, except SR29 and SR26, which bridge a whole ladder.
// A motor pair is two armatures in series, then both fields inside the reverser
// (NW1-NW4, NW5-NW8: field side), with six shunt steps SPn + RPn and the inductive
// shunt I across reverser and fields together. OS1/OS3 isolate a pair, OS2/OS4 pass it by.
//
// LAYOUT: the compiler cannot turn a corner, so every node is a vertical bus and every
// element has a row of its own. This text was read back by a port of circuit_compiler.cs
// and gives the same netlist it was drawn from.
//
// NUMBERS: starting resistors designed by design_resistors.py, scaled; field shunts worked out from
// the DTR's percentages; supply and pantograph still placeholders. See docs/NOTES.md.
// NOT in here: SDS1/RDS1 and SDS2/RDS2 (a shunt to the mid-point of each field pair),
// the voltage relays across the armatures, the ammeter shunts.

